<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Miguel Malvar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1865–1911</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Miguel Malvar was a Filipino general from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batangas">Batangas</a> who fought in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippine-revolution">Philippine Revolution</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippine-american-war">Philippine–American War</a>. After the capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emilio-aguinaldo">Emilio Aguinaldo</a> in 1901 he led the continuing resistance as commander of the revolutionary forces, conducting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> warfare in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luzon">Luzon</a>. He was the last major Filipino general to surrender, in April 1902, after an American campaign that devastated Batangas.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/miguel-malvar.jpg" alt="Miguel Malvar" width="253" height="300" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jose N. Sevilla · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Miguel_malvar_PG.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
